TEXT HEAD:
Batch Experiments
Controlled model experiments
Execute deterministic parameter sweeps and comparative A/B studies across multiple pseudorandom seeds.
Parameter Sweep
Comparative A/B
Topology packets use timed injection and a 100,000 µs drain. TCP/UDP run bulk transfers to completion (duration is not a cutoff); they do not model scheduled faults or stochastic link loss. Transport requires links ≥1 Mbps and delay ≥100 µs. Seeds do not randomize transport runs. TCP latency is an RTT/2 estimate; UDP latency and jitter are unavailable (zero placeholders), not measured zero delay. Other protocols use their dedicated studios.
